  "author_association": "MEMBER",
  "body": "### ESLint version\n\nv9.x\n\n### What problem do you want to solve?\n\n`eslint` v9.x versions are not deprecated on npm, only older versions are. Now that v9.x has reached end-of-life, we may consider deprecating v9.x versions as well.\n\n### What do you think is the correct solution?\n\nDeprecate ESLint v9.x packages on npm. This is a follow-up on #18972.\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to work on this change.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [x] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\nNo pull request is needed for this change. The packages can be deprecated by logging in to npm as user eslintbot and running:\n\n```shell\nnpm deprecate \"eslint@<10\" \"This version is no longer supported. Please see https://eslint.org/version-support for other options.\"\n```\n\nSee #18972 for more context.",
